Let me look at the `tls_decrypt_ticket` function again. The key path is:

```c
sess = d2i_SSL_SESSION(NULL, &p, slen);
slen -= p - sdec;
OPENSSL_free(sdec);
if (sess) {
    if (slen != 0) {
        SSL_SESSION_free(sess);
        ret = SSL_TICKET_NO_DECRYPT;
        goto end;
    }
```

When `slen != 0`, `sess` is freed but not set to NULL. Then `*psess = sess` at `end` sets the dangling pointer.

But to trigger this, we need a valid ticket that decrypts successfully. This requires knowing the ticket keys.

